Laurent Deniel  <deniel@fr.airsysatm.thomson-csf.com> wrote:
} If someone has the source code of Digital UNIX 3.2 or 4.0, 
} can you have a look at the semop system call implementation 
} for telling me all the reasons the semop may have to fail with 
} the ERANGE error code. I checked all sem UNDO-related system
} kernel parameters (and the semval value is less than the
} system-imposed limit), I do not see any reason of such a 
} failure ...

   Looking at the V4.0(b) source, I believe the man
   page for "semop" to be accurate:

      [ERANGE]  An operation caused a semval to overflow the system-defined
      limit, or an operation caused an adjust-on-exit value to exceed
      the system-defined limit.

   The relevant lines look like this:

      if (op->sem_op > 0) {
        if (op->sem_op + (long) semp->semval > seminfo.semvmx ...
           return (ERANGE);

      if (val >  seminfo.semaem ||
          val < -seminfo.semaem) return (ERANGE);

      if (uentp->uent_aoe >  seminfo.semaem ||
          uentp->uent_aoe < -seminfo.semaem) ... return (ERANGE);


John
