Free? Well we did get DEC's power monitoring CD with the DU 4.0, but I'm not
sure which UPSs it refers to. All of them have DEC mark, but what are the DEC's
UPSs?

On the other hand, APC has a software package called PowerCHUTE plus, which has
support for (among other) DEC OSF/1. We install it with Digital UNIX 3.2G and
4.0D and it works. It has a functional X Windows GUI and lets you specify all
those nice things, like actions for events:

- UPS on battery (power failure)
- UPS on battery & battery low (running out of battery)
- Automatic turn-on delay
.......

It also keeps log of all events, like brownouts, sags, overvoltages, ...

BTW, on DEC OSF/1 and Digital UNIX Back-UPS IS NOT SUPPORTED by PowerCHUTE. Of
course, Smart-UPS and Matrix-UPS are OK.

And of course, you'll need a smart-signalling cable (black one). It should come
with the UPS, but I'm not sure.

It's worth the money.

CU,
Nix.




